-- Scenario tests, read against the English text (`the English text`); where the Vietnamese
-- answers differently, the test is in pc-travel-tests-en-vi.l4. Every expected value was
-- worked by hand from the clause cited above it, before the rule was run. Thresholds are
-- tested on both sides; each exclusion has a case that triggers it and a near miss.
-- Dates: the base Period of Insurance is 1-20 April 2026, the trip departs 1 April 2026.

§ `Terms and conditions applying to all sections`

§§ `Clauses 1 and 16`
#ASSERT `clause 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` `the test case`
#ASSERT NOT `clause 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` (`the test case with conditions` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `clause 1 — the conditions precedent to liability are met` (`the test case with conditions` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the general terms let a claim proceed` `the English text` `the test case` `1A Medical Expenses` (YMD 2026 4 5) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `the general terms let a claim proceed` `the English text` (`the test case with conditions` FALSE TRUE FALSE) `1A Medical Expenses` (YMD 2026 4 5) EMPTY
#ASSERT `clause 16 — the Policy is void and no claim is payable` (`the test case with conditions` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the general terms let a claim proceed` `the English text` (`the test case with conditions` TRUE TRUE TRUE) `1A Medical Expenses` (YMD 2026 4 5) EMPTY
#ASSERT `clause 16 — the Company may deny the claim` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `clause 16 — the Company may deny the claim` FALSE

