§ `Section 1A — Medical Expenses`

`three expenses on 6 April` MEANS
    LIST `an expense of` `hospitalization` 10_000_000 `on` (YMD 2026 4 6)
       , `an expense of` `hospital room and board, charged on a per diem basis` 8_000_000 `on` (YMD 2026 4 6)
       , `an expense of` `consultation by registered doctors` 2_000_000 `on` (YMD 2026 4 6)

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF `A medical expense`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`1A pays, for an Illness on 5 April, for` xs MEANS
    `1A — the amount payable` `the English text` `the test case` (`a Medical Expenses claim for` `an Illness on 5 April` `of` xs `unable to return` FALSE)

GIVEN x IS A `A medical expense`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`1A pays, for an Illness on 5 April, for the one expense` x MEANS
    `1A pays, for an Illness on 5 April, for` (LIST x)

-- 1A.1(a): room and board per diem is capped at 6,000,000 a day: 10 + 6 + 2.
#ASSERT `1A pays, for an Illness on 5 April, for` `three expenses on 6 April` EQUALS 18_000_000
#ASSERT `1A pays, for an Illness on 5 April, for the one expense` (`an expense of` `hospital room and board, charged on a per diem basis` 6_000_000 `on` (YMD 2026 4 6)) EQUALS 6_000_000
