§ `The hostile reading, demonstrated`

-- F-PA-NOTICE: an Accident on 5 April; death on 5 October. Section 2 pays (death within 12
-- calendar months), but CP 1's notice period closed on 20 May, 138 days before the death.
`a death on 5 October from an Accident on 5 April` MEANS
    `a Personal Accident claim for` `Accidental Death` `with` `a full disablement` `, the Accident on` (YMD 2026 4 5) `, the loss on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `, on board` NOTHING `, a benefit already payable` FALSE
#ASSERT `2 pays, in the test case, for` `a death on 5 October from an Accident on 5 April` EQUALS 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `CP 1 — the last day to give notice of the claim` `the test case` (`notice given on` NOTHING) BELOW YMD 2026 10 5
#ASSERT Day (YMD 2026 10 5) MINUS Day (`CP 1 — the last day to give notice of the claim` `the test case` (`notice given on` NOTHING)) EQUALS 138
-- F-PA-NOTICE, Permanent Total Disablement: the definition needs 52 consecutive weeks, so
-- the disablement cannot be shown before 4 April 2027, long after 20 May 2026.
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 4 5 PLUS 52 TIMES 7) GREATER THAN `CP 1 — the last day to give notice of the claim` `the test case` (`notice given on` NOTHING)
-- F-NOTICE-LATE, section 1A.1(b): after a return on 15 April, follow-up expenses on 14 July
-- are covered (asserted above, 40 million), and the notice period closed on 20 May.
#ASSERT `CP 1 — the last day to give notice of the claim` `the test case, returned on 15 April` (`notice given on` NOTHING) BELOW YMD 2026 7 14
#ASSERT `1A — the amount payable` `the English text` `the test case, returned on 15 April` (`a Medical Expenses claim for` `an Illness on 5 April` `of` (LIST `a follow-up at home of` 40_000_000 `on` (YMD 2026 7 14)) `unable to return` FALSE) EQUALS 40_000_000

-- F-24H: a passport stolen on 6 April, missed until 8 April, reported 10 hours after the
-- Insured Person knew. Section 5.1 counts from awareness and is met; CP 2(c) wants reports
-- "within 24 hours of the occurrence" (58 hours here) and is not.
#ASSERT `5 — the amount payable` `the English text` `the test case` (`a passport lost by` `theft` `, reported after` (JUST 10) `hours, as soon as practicable` TRUE `, left unattended` FALSE) EQUALS 15_000_000
#ASSERT NOT `CP 2(c) — the report to the relevant authorities was within 24 hours` 58
